118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E ( Our city is located in Northern Austria, and we experience a cold winter climate along with occasional hot summer heat waves. The climate affects and changes the building style. Transportation will be affected due to the abundance of snow; cyclists won't be able to ride in the cold climate. To adapt to Carzanart's snowy climate, we developed specialized winter bicycle wheels created to grip icy terrain. This allows people to cycle all the way through the city year-round while reducing energy use and pollution from motorized vehicles. We can incorporate excess heat from power plants to heat homes. Despite the limited need for cooling in Carzanart, we will still have the St. Car River system along with transpiration from plants to help regulate the occasional hot summer temperatures.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
