/T (Human Impact & Sustainability)
/E (Human Impact & Sustainability)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E ( Carzanart faces environmental difficulties year-round due to the cold and snowy climate including frozen rivers, avalanches, and flooding. Our city reduces and minimizes these problems by keeping around heating systems and manufacturing more coats for people going outside. These coats will be made out of sealed biomass, a biodegradable material under conditions. To fight the avalanches, dams were installed and avalanche tests were run on the main parts of the mountain. We proceed with these strategies to identify and reduce the amount of avalanches or damage. For residential areas near Mt. Neverest, we designed bunkers to survive avalanches. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E ( For us to reduce the amount of fossil fuels used, we recommend bikes to people or use public transit to bring down air pollution and global warming. We will also counter air pollution with plants to absorb CO2. We incorporated visible signs that the forest had been reduced to the north due to human impact; it previously covered the area of the city and was reduced to create houses, like in modern-day cities. To sustainably get energy, we choose to use renewable energy by utilizing solar and hydro sources. To source solar energy, we utilize the high altitude of Mt. Neverest and the highly reflective, white snow.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
